# NI Brain learning (required on deployable work)

NI Brain is the Northside Intelligence knowledge base (Supabase project `kxijunwgbrlfzvgkhklo`). Match Fit must continuously teach it how Northside tools are built.

## When to record

On any task that ships schema, architecture, workflows, or notable product logic:

1. After finishing, call or extend `@/lib/ni-brain-client` helpers (`recordNiBrainLearning`, `recordNiBrainDecision`, `recordNiBrainBuildEvent`) when the change is architectural or operational.
2. Run `npm run ni-brain:sync` when Prisma models, migrations, or core `src/lib/*` patterns change materially.
3. Version bumps already log via `npm run version:bump` → `scripts/ni-brain-record-version.mjs`.

## What to upload

- Schema summaries (model names, migration ids), portal/workflow decisions, lib module conventions
- Operator learnings (content calendar edits, outreach tone/outcomes)
- Product version + reason from `version:bump`

## Never upload

- Passwords, API keys, JWTs, `DATABASE_URL`, Stripe secrets, user PII
- Full source dumps — summarize patterns and decisions only
- Raw `.env` contents

## Env (server + scripts)

```bash
NI_BRAIN_SUPABASE_URL=https://kxijunwgbrlfzvgkhklo.supabase.co
NI_BRAIN_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role from Northside Intelligence Brain only>
```

The service role JWT `ref` must be `kxijunwgbrlfzvgkhklo` — not the Match Fit app project (`qtesdsxrfggdlxdaraaq`).

## Tables

| Table | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `Context` | `MATCH FIT — BUILD CONTEXT` auto-sync |
| `Learnings` | Distilled lessons |
| `Decisions` | Architecture / product decisions |
| `arm3_weekly_logs` | Build events (`tool_slug`: `match-fit`) |
| `match_fit_content_*` | Content calendar |

## Completion

On deployable tasks, state whether NI Brain was updated (sync run, learning recorded, or skipped because keys unset).
